  "question": {
    "text": "If \\(f(x)=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}\\), then (fof of \\()(x)\\) is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{\\sqrt{1+3 \\mathrm{x}^2}}\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{3 x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "None of these",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "\\(\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{\\sqrt{1+\\mathrm{x}^2}}\\)\n\\((f o f)(x)=\\frac{\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+x^2}}}{\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x^2}{1+x^2}}}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2 x^2+1}}\\)\n\\((fofof)(x)=\\frac{\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{2 x^2+1}}}{\\sqrt{1+\\frac{x^2}{2 x^2+1}}}=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+3 x^2}}\\)"
  }
}